data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Let `W` be the warmup length and `T` the total length. For `step < W`, the rate is the base rate times\n`step / W`. For `W <= step < T`, measure progress `p` from zero at `W` to one at `T`, then blend from\nthe base rate down to the floor with the factor `(1 + cos(pi * p)) / 2`. At `step >= T`, return the floor."},"hints_note":null}

